---
import AdminLayout from '../../layouts/AdminLayout.astro';
---

<AdminLayout
  title="Journalist Outreach | ProtectMyMobile Admin"
  description="Email templates and outreach tools for journalists and media contacts."
  currentPage="outreach"
>
  <div class="p-3 sm:p-4 lg:p-8">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-6 sm:mb-8">
      <h1 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-foreground">Journalist Outreach</h1>
      <p class="text-neutral-600 text-xs sm:text-sm mt-1 sm:mt-2">
        Pre-written templates for pitching data stories, embargoed releases, and follow-ups.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Templates Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:gap-6">

      <!-- Template 1: Quarterly Data Release -->
      <div class="bg-card rounded-xl shadow-md p-4 sm:p-6 border-t-4 border-primary">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
          <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Quarterly Data Release</h2>
          <button 
            class="copy-btn text-xs bg-primary text-white px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg hover:bg-primary-hover transition-colors"
            data-target="template-quarterly"
          >
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-neutral-50 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-neutral-700 font-mono whitespace-pre-wrap" id="template-quarterly">Subject: EMBARGOED: UK Mobile Phone Theft Data – Q[QUARTER] [YEAR] / ProtectMyMobile

Hi [NAME],

I'm writing to offer you an embargoed look at our latest quarterly mobile phone theft data, collected via Freedom of Information requests to all 43 UK police forces.

**Key headline findings:**
• [FORCE NAME] saw a [X]% [increase/decrease] in reported thefts compared to the previous quarter
• The total number of mobile phone thefts reported UK-wide was [NUMBER]
• [BOROUGH/AREA] remains the highest-risk area in [CITY] with [NUMBER] incidents

**What we have:**
- Force-by-force breakdown (CSV + interactive charts)
- Month-by-month trends for the last 12 months
- Borough-level data for London, Manchester, Birmingham, and Glasgow
- Comparison with device recovery rates where available

**Embargo:** [DATE] at [TIME] – we'd love to give you a 48-hour head start.

The data is available exclusively at https://protectmymobile.xyz/statistics

Happy to jump on a quick call or send over the raw data if useful.

Best,
[YOUR NAME]
ProtectMyMobile Research Team
https://protectmymobile.xyz

---

*ProtectMyMobile is an independent UK consumer resource tracking mobile phone theft trends via FOI requests and crowdsourced reports.*</div>
      </div>

      <!-- Template 2: Specific Story Pitch -->
      <div class="bg-card rounded-xl shadow-md p-4 sm:p-6 border-t-4 border-blue-500">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
          <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Specific Story Pitch</h2>
          <button 
            class="copy-btn text-xs bg-blue-500 text-white px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg hover:bg-primary transition-colors"
            data-target="template-pitch"
          >
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-neutral-50 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-neutral-700 font-mono whitespace-pre-wrap" id="template-pitch">Subject: Story idea: [ANGLE] / ProtectMyMobile data

Hi [NAME],

I saw your recent piece on [RELATED TOPIC] and thought this might be a good fit for a follow-up.

We've just published [SPECIFIC DATA POINT] that I think your readers would find striking:

**The angle:** [ONE SENTENCE HOOK]

**The data:**
- [BULLET 1]
- [BULLET 2]
- [BULLET 3]

**Visuals available:**
- Interactive map: https://protectmymobile.xyz/theft-map
- Location-specific stats: https://protectmymobile.xyz/[location]
- Full data dashboard: https://protectmymobile.xyz/statistics

All data is sourced from verified FOI responses and crowdsourced reports. Happy to provide raw CSVs, custom charts, or a quote for the piece.

Let me know if you'd like any of the above.

Best,
[YOUR NAME]
ProtectMyMobile
https://protectmymobile.xyz</div>
      </div>

      <!-- Template 3: Reactive / Newsjacking -->
      <div class="bg-card rounded-xl shadow-md p-4 sm:p-6 border-t-4 border-amber-500">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
          <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Reactive / Newsjacking</h2>
          <button 
            class="copy-btn text-xs bg-amber-500 text-white px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg hover:bg-warning transition-colors"
            data-target="template-reactive"
          >
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-neutral-50 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-neutral-700 font-mono whitespace-pre-wrap" id="template-reactive">Subject: Data on [INCIDENT/AREA] – quick comment?

Hi [NAME],

Following the news about [INCIDENT], I wanted to flag that we have specific data on mobile phone theft in [AREA] that might add context to your coverage.

**Quick stats:**
• [NUMBER] thefts reported in [AREA] in the last 12 months
• That's [X]% [above/below] the national average per capita
• Peak times: [TIME/DAY if known]

**What we're seeing:** [ONE SENTENCE ANALYSIS]

I can provide:
- A quote for your piece
- Borough-level breakdown
- Comparison with neighbouring areas

All data is from verified police FOI responses. Let me know if useful – happy to turn this around in under an hour.

Best,
[YOUR NAME]
ProtectMyMobile
https://protectmymobile.xyz</div>
      </div>

      <!-- Template 4: Follow-up / Relationship -->
      <div class="bg-card rounded-xl shadow-md p-4 sm:p-6 border-t-4 border-green-500">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
          <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Follow-up / Relationship</h2>
          <button 
            class="copy-btn text-xs bg-green-500 text-white px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg hover:bg-green-600 transition-colors"
            data-target="template-followup"
          >
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-neutral-50 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-neutral-700 font-mono whitespace-pre-wrap" id="template-followup">Subject: Next quarter's data + a heads up

Hi [NAME],

Hope you're well. Just a quick note that we're pulling together Q[NEXT QUARTER] data this week and I wanted to flag a couple of stories brewing:

**Coming up:**
1. [STORY ANGLE 1] – data looks significant
2. [STORY ANGLE 2] – early numbers suggest [TREND]

If any of those sound like they'd work for [PUBLICATION], I can send over a preview before we publish.

Also: we've just launched a crowdsourced theft map (https://protectmymobile.xyz/theft-map) that's starting to show interesting patterns beyond the official stats. Worth a look.

No pressure – just wanted you on the list first.

Best,
[YOUR NAME]
ProtectMyMobile
https://protectmymobile.xyz</div>
      </div>

      <!-- Template 5: Press Release Format -->
      <div class="bg-card rounded-xl shadow-md p-4 sm:p-6 border-t-4 border-purple-500 lg:col-span-2">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
          <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Press Release (Full Format)</h2>
          <button 
            class="copy-btn text-xs bg-purple-500 text-white px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg hover:bg-purple-600 transition-colors"
            data-target="template-pressrelease"
          >
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-neutral-50 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-neutral-700 font-mono whitespace-pre-wrap" id="template-pressrelease">FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE

**[HEADLINE]: UK Mobile Phone Thefts [TREND] by [X]% in Q[QUARTER] [YEAR]**

*New Freedom of Information data reveals [KEY FINDING]*

[LONDON/DATE] – ProtectMyMobile, the UK's independent mobile phone theft tracking resource, today published its Q[QUARTER] [YEAR] analysis of mobile phone theft data obtained via Freedom of Information requests to all UK police forces.

**Key Findings:**

• **[STAT 1]**: [FORCE/AREA] recorded [NUMBER] mobile phone thefts in Q[QUARTER], making it the [highest/lowest] in [REGION/the UK].
• **[STAT 2]**: Overall, UK police forces recorded [NUMBER] mobile phone thefts in Q[QUARTER], a [X]% [increase/decrease] from Q[PREVIOUS QUARTER].
• **[STAT 3]**: [SPECIFIC INSIGHT, e.g. "London boroughs accounted for X% of all UK thefts"].

**[QUOTE FROM FOUNDER/SPOKESPERSON]:**

"[QUOTE]. This data shows [INSIGHT]. We urge [CALL TO ACTION]."

**Methodology:**
ProtectMyMobile submits Freedom of Information requests to all 43 UK police forces on a quarterly basis. Data is verified, normalised, and published alongside crowdsourced reports from victims at https://protectmymobile.xyz/theft-map.

**Resources for journalists:**
- Full data dashboard: https://protectmymobile.xyz/statistics
- Interactive theft map: https://protectmymobile.xyz/theft-map
- Location-specific guides: https://protectmymobile.xyz/[location]
- Emergency guide: https://protectmymobile.xyz/emergency

**Contact:**
[YOUR NAME]
[EMAIL]
[PHONE]
https://protectmymobile.xyz

###

**About ProtectMyMobile:**
ProtectMyMobile is an independent UK consumer resource that tracks mobile phone theft trends through Freedom of Information requests, publishes location-specific safety guides, and provides free emergency resources for victims. Founded in [YEAR], the platform has processed [NUMBER] FOI requests and crowdsourced [NUMBER] victim reports.

---

*Note to editors: All data is available under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0. Please credit ProtectMyMobile (protectmymobile.xyz) when using these statistics.*</div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- Tips Section -->
    <div class="mt-6 sm:mt-8 bg-card rounded-xl shadow-md p-4 sm:p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4">Outreach Tips</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-neutral-700">
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary mr-2 font-bold">1.</span>
            <span><strong>Embargo everything</strong> — Give journalists 24–48 hours exclusivity. They ignore mass press releases.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary mr-2 font-bold">2.</span>
            <span><strong>Lead with one stat</strong> — Don't bury the headline. The first sentence should be the story.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary mr-2 font-bold">3.</span>
            <span><strong>Attach a chart</strong> — Journalists are visual. A simple bar chart doubles your response rate.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-neutral-700">
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary mr-2 font-bold">4.</span>
            <span><strong>Target local first</strong> — Local BBC radio and Metro newspapers pick up data stories faster than nationals.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary mr-2 font-bold">5.</span>
            <span><strong>Follow up once</strong> — If no reply in 48 hours, one polite follow-up. Then move on.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary mr-2 font-bold">6.</span>
            <span><strong>Build a list</strong> — Keep a spreadsheet of who covered you. They're your warm leads next quarter.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll('.copy-btn').forEach(btn => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const targetId = btn.getAttribute('data-target');
        const text = document.getElementById(targetId!)!.textContent || '';
        navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(() => {
          const original = btn.textContent;
          btn.textContent = 'Copied!';
          setTimeout(() => btn.textContent = original, 1500);
        });
      });
    });
  </script>
</AdminLayout>
